{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"c40143ae55fecfab","name":"card_unit_fieseler_156","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/WorldAtWar/units/card_unit_fieseler_156","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"FIESELER FI 156","text":"At the end of your turn, activate a random Countermeasure in hand.","flavorText":"The Fieseler Fi 156 Storch (e. stork) was a German liaison aircraft that was used by the Luftwaffe during WWII. The aircraft was designed to be versatile; it didn’t need a long runway and it had foldable wings which made it easy to transport by trailers or by being towed by vehicles. During WWII it was used by the Luftwaffe in all major theaters and perhaps most famously during the daring German commando rescue of Benito Mussolini in 1943. Over 2,900 Fi 156 Storch were built between 1937-1945, including variants, and the production for private use continued in France and Czechoslovakia after the war. Around 60 FI 156 were captured by the Allies during the war and one was assigned to Field Marshal Bernard Montgomery as his personal transport.","faction":"Germany","type":"fighter","rarity":"Rare","cost":3,"operationCost":1,"attack":1,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_fieseler_156","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_fieseler_156_title","SourceString":"FIESELER FI 156","LocalizedString":"FIESELER FI 156"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::fighter","attack":1,"defense":3,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_fieseler_156_text","SourceString":"At the end of your turn, activate a random Countermeasure in hand.","LocalizedString":"At the end of your turn, activate a random Countermeasure in hand."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_fieseler_156_history","SourceString":"The Fieseler Fi 156 Storch (e. stork) was a German liaison aircraft that was used by the Luftwaffe during WWII. The aircraft was designed to be versatile; it didn’t need a long runway and it had foldable wings which made it easy to transport by trailers or by being towed by vehicles. During WWII it was used by the Luftwaffe in all major theaters and perhaps most famously during the daring German commando rescue of Benito Mussolini in 1943. Over 2,900 Fi 156 Storch were built between 1937-1945, including variants, and the production for private use continued in France and Czechoslovakia after the war. Around 60 FI 156 were captured by the Allies during the war and one was assigned to Field Marshal Bernard Montgomery as his personal transport.","LocalizedString":"The Fieseler Fi 156 Storch (e. stork) was a German liaison aircraft that was used by the Luftwaffe during WWII. The aircraft was designed to be versatile; it didn’t need a long runway and it had foldable wings which made it easy to transport by trailers or by being towed by vehicles. During WWII it was used by the Luftwaffe in all major theaters and perhaps most famously during the daring German commando rescue of Benito Mussolini in 1943. Over 2,900 Fi 156 Storch were built between 1937-1945, including variants, and the production for private use continued in France and Czechoslovakia after the war. Around 60 FI 156 were captured by the Allies during the war and one was assigned to Field Marshal Bernard Montgomery as his personal transport."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WorldAtWar","isReserved":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnEndOfTurn"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Trigger"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'AU_depl_biplane_Cue'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Biplane/AU_depl_biplane_Cue.0"},"soundMoveToFrontline":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'AU_move_biplane_01_Cue'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Biplane/AU_move_biplane_01_Cue.0"},"soundAttack":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'AU_move_biplane_01_Cue'","ObjectPath":"kards/Co